    *   *Draft 1:* My old laptop suddenly stopped charging last week, the dreaded black screen of death. Instead of tossing it or buying a new one, I opened the chassis and found a simple blown capacitor on the charging board. I ordered a replacement part for five dollars, and now it's running faster than ever. This is exactly why I love repairable hardware. There's something deeply satisfying about saving a piece of technology from the landfill instead of contributing to e-waste.

